# PLACEHOLDER test scene for the dialogue player and screen (0702, 0704),
# with a reply choice and lead tokens (0708). Uses the placeholder
# characters from data/characters.ron; the real Chapter 1 script (0707)
# goes in its own files.

@scene test
@caption Village of Heth, dusk
> The rain had not stopped for three days.
@left  test_lord neutral
@right test_knight angry
test_knight: You're late.
test_lord[happy]: Better late than... well.
test_knight: Than never. Say it.
  I've heard it from you often enough.
@right clear
> The knight stamps off into the rain.
@right test_archer surprised
test_archer: Was that about me?
test_lord[sad]: It's always about you.
@left lead neutral
test_archer: {lead}! You came back for us.
@choice
* earnest: I said I would. I keep my word.
  test_archer[happy]: You do. It's why we follow you.
* wry: Someone has to carry your arrows.
  test_archer[angry]: I carry my own arrows, thank you.
  > The archer's ears go red anyway.
* blunt: Get moving. We're not safe here.
  test_archer: Right. Moving.
@endchoice
@right test_archer neutral
lead: Let's move.
> {lead} tightens {their} grip on the sword. {They} won't lose anyone today.
@end
